From: songhyunho1111 <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Subject: ipc/msg: keep expelled receivers from taking new messages
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:28:21 +0900

Patch series "ipc/msg: prevent reads after queue permission revocation".

A process whose read access to a SysV message queue was revoked by
IPC_SET can receive a message sent afterward. A blocked receiver needs
no capability and can have a different UID from the queue owner. Patch 1
prevents delivery to a receiver awakened by IPC_SET. Patch 2 closes the
window between the read permission check and waiter insertion.

IPC_SET continues to wake every blocked receiver, whether its access
changed or not. A receiver with unchanged access leaves and rejoins the
wait list after waking, potentially changing its position as before.
A sender can queue a message instead of handing it to that receiver.


This patch (of 2):

IPC_SET sets a blocked receiver's result to -EAGAIN so it retries its
read permission check. expunge_all() leaves the receiver on q_receivers;
a sender can hand it a new message before it wakes. If IPC_SET revoked
its read access, it receives data that was sent after the revocation.

Mark every receiver that expunge_all() touched and skip it in
pipelined_send(). Keep it linked until it wakes so IPC_RMID can still
find it and change its result to -EIDRM. The message remains queued. After waking, a receiver whose access
was revoked gets -EACCES. The wake-all behavior and possible wait-list
reordering on IPC_SET remain.

Signed-off-by: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reported-by: Hyunho Song <songhh06101@gmail.com>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/r/CAJ5=Bnt42P4J_t_4=hUSsAd-WWNSoxendooYm8aTLFjyZqAh=Q@mail.gmail.com
Reviewed-by: Manfred Spraul <manfred@colorfullife.com>
Tested-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
  Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261120153057.f1b13f748c4876044c706449@linux-foundation.org
Cc: Davidlohr Bueso <dave@stgolabs.net>
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>

 ipc/msg.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/ipc/msg.c
+++ b/ipc/msg.c
@@ -82,6 +82,7 @@
 	long			r_maxsize;
 
 	struct msg_msg		*r_msg;
+	bool			r_expunge;
 };
 
 /* one msg_sender for each sleeping sender */
@@ -255,6 +256,8 @@
 		struct task_struct *r_tsk;
 
 		r_tsk = get_task_struct(msr->r_tsk);
+		/* IPC_RMID must still find this waiter and set -EIDRM. */
+		msr->r_expunge = true;
 
 		/* see MSG_BARRIER for purpose/pairing */
 		smp_store_release(&msr->r_msg, ERR_PTR(res));
@@ -819,6 +822,9 @@
 	struct msg_receiver *msr, *t;
 
 	list_for_each_entry_safe(msr, t, &msq->q_receivers, r_list) {
+		/* IPC_SET needs the receiver to recheck its access. */
+		if (msr->r_expunge)
+			continue;
 		if (testmsg(msg, msr->r_msgtype, msr->r_mode) &&
 		    !security_msg_queue_msgrcv(&msq->q_perm, msg, msr->r_tsk,
 					       msr->r_msgtype, msr->r_mode)) {
@@ -1178,6 +1184,7 @@
 			goto out_unlock0;
 		}
 
+		msr_d.r_expunge = false;
 		list_add_tail(&msr_d.r_list, &msq->q_receivers);
 		msr_d.r_tsk = current;
 		msr_d.r_msgtype = msgtyp;
